WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.304
Use the school sequence aloud: technical quality, rate, regularity, P waves, PR and QRS measurements, then ST and T review with QT when indicated. A familiar-looking rhythm is not permission to skip the later checks, particularly medication risk or changing ST findings.
按学校顺序口述：技术质量、心率、规则性、P 波、PR 和 QRS 测量，然后复核 ST、T，必要时测 QT。节律看起来熟悉，也不能省略后续检查，尤其药物风险或变化中的 ST 表现。

00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:40.344
The order structures reporting; it does not replace rapid patient assessment. Check responsiveness, breathing, circulation and instability before a leisurely strip analysis. If there is no effective circulation, follow the applicable resuscitation pathway instead of completing a classroom worksheet first.
这个顺序组织报告，但不能替代快速患者评估。详细分析条带前，应先检查反应、呼吸、循环和不稳定表现；若没有有效循环，应按适用复苏流程行动，不能先填完课堂表格。

00:00:40.344 --> 00:00:59.664
Confirm that this is the right patient and a current tracing. Check speed, gain, calibration and whether intended leads are available. Look for baseline movement, signal dropout or interference. These checks prevent a technical distortion being promoted into a clinical diagnosis.
确认患者身份和记录时效，核对纸速、增益、校准及所需导联是否齐全，并寻找基线漂移、信号脱落或干扰。这些检查可防止把技术失真升级为临床诊断。

00:00:59.664 --> 00:01:17.352
Repeat an uninterpretable tracing after correcting the cause when feasible. Record any persistent limitation. Do not delay assessment or time-critical treatment while trying to produce a perfect printout, and do not claim a reliable interpretation of obscured waveforms.
在可行时纠正原因并重取无法判读的记录，记录持续存在的局限。不要为了完美打印而延误评估或紧急处置，也不能声称已可靠判读被遮蔽的波形。

00:01:17.352 --> 00:01:34.200
Calculate the ventricular rate using the method that fits the observed regularity. Then describe whether the pattern is regular, repeats an irregular grouping, or has no repeating RR pattern. Use a longer sample or calipers when the distinction is unclear.
根据观察到的规则性选择方法计算心室率，再说明节律是规则、以重复分组方式不规则，还是 RR 没有重复模式。区别不清时，可使用更长记录或卡尺。

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:57.264
Count atrial activity separately when P or flutter waves outnumber QRS complexes. A ventricular rate alone cannot reveal the atrial-to-ventricular conduction ratio. Conversely, an irregularly irregular RR pattern is not enough to diagnose atrial fibrillation unless atrial activity and technical quality support it.
当 P 波或扑动波多于 QRS 时，应另外计算心房活动。单凭心室率不能知道房室传导比例；同样，只有 RR 绝对不齐还不足以诊断房颤，必须有心房活动及技术质量的支持。

00:01:57.264 --> 00:02:15.384
Inspect more than one beat and, when useful, another lead. Ask whether P waves are visible, whether their shape is consistent, and whether there is a reliable relationship to each QRS. P waves may be buried in T waves or rapid complexes rather than truly absent.
应查看不止一个搏动，必要时参考其他导联。判断 P 波是否可见、形态是否一致、与每个 QRS 是否有可靠关系。P 波可能埋在 T 波或快速波群中，并不一定真正缺失。

00:02:15.384 --> 00:02:36.432
Look in both directions: is every QRS preceded by an appropriate P, and is every P followed by a QRS? The second question detects failed conduction that a glance at conducted beats misses. Independent P and QRS schedules raise a different question from merely changing P-wave shape.
要双向检查：每个 QRS 前是否有合适 P 波，每个 P 后是否都有 QRS？第二个问题能发现只看下传搏动时容易漏掉的传导失败。P、QRS 各走各的，与单纯 P 形态改变是不同问题。

00:02:36.432 --> 00:02:55.608
Measure PR in conducted beats and compare successive intervals. Measure QRS width rather than describing it by visual impression alone. At the recovery step, examine ST displacement and T-wave changes; a normal-looking rhythm name does not complete this part of the assessment.
在已下传搏动中测 PR 并比较连续间期；QRS 宽度也应实测，不能只凭视觉印象。复极步骤要查看 ST 偏移及 T 波改变；说出看似正常的节律名称，并不等于完成该步骤。

00:02:55.608 --> 00:03:17.952
Record unclear boundaries and acquisition limitations. QTc deserves attention in syncope, medication exposure or a suspicious recovery pattern. Detailed diagnostic twelve-lead patterns belong to the later school course; recognizing a concerning finding here should trigger appropriate communication, not an invented diagnosis.
记录边界不清和采集局限。晕厥、药物暴露或可疑复极表现时，应关注 QTc。精细诊断性十二导联形态属于学校后续课程；本课发现异常应促成适当沟通，不能编造诊断。

00:03:17.952 --> 00:03:37.608
On this original example, verified settings and a clean strip show a regular ventricular rate of ninety, consistent P waves before each QRS, PR zero point one eight seconds and QRS zero point one zero seconds. Describe those observations before applying the sinus-rhythm label.
这个原创例子设置已核实、记录清晰，心室率规则为每分钟90次，每个 QRS 前有一致 P 波，PR 为0.18秒，QRS 为0.10秒。应先描述这些观察，再使用窦性节律名称。

00:03:37.608 --> 00:03:58.032
Complete the report with what was not established: absence of obvious ST change in one monitoring lead does not exclude ACS. Add symptoms, pulse, perfusion, whether a diagnostic recording was obtained, and the reassessment plan. This is a reasoned interpretation, not just a rhythm name.
报告还应说明没有确定什么：某个监护导联未见明显 ST 改变，并不能排除 ACS。补充症状、脉搏、灌注、是否取得诊断记录及复评计划，才是有依据的判读，而不只是节律名称。
